                        "markdownDescription": "Native critic rule IDs to disable (e.g. `native.common.assignment_in_condition`)."
                    },
                    "perl-lsp.perlcritic.enabled": {
                        "type": "boolean",
                        "default": false,
                        "scope": "resource",
                        "order": 40,
                        "deprecationMessage": "Deprecated: use perl-lsp.critic.enabled (with perl-lsp.critic.engine = \"legacy\" for the external binary). This alias still works but perl-lsp.critic.* wins if both are set.",
                        "markdownDeprecationMessage": "**Deprecated:** use `perl-lsp.critic.enabled` (with `perl-lsp.critic.engine` = `legacy` for the external binary). This alias still works but `perl-lsp.critic.*` wins if both are set.",
                        "description": "Enable the optional external perlcritic diagnostics for legacy compatibility. Native critic diagnostics are on by default; this setting only takes effect when the critic engine is set to legacy in .perl-lsp.toml (the perlcritic binary must then be on PATH).",
                        "markdownDescription": "Enable the optional external `perlcritic` diagnostics for legacy compatibility. Native critic diagnostics are always on by default; this setting only takes effect when `[critic].engine = \"legacy\"` is set in `.perl-lsp.toml`, in which case the `perlcritic` binary must be on `PATH`."
                    },
